---
description: Explain the difference between current and prior editions without conflating boundary change with performance.
args: { dossier: ReportingDossier; boundary: ReportingBoundary; reconciliation: ReconciliationLedger }
returns: string[]
---
Compare the latest accepted edition with the new measure and boundary versions. Attribute each affected difference to a changed boundary, corrected source, meter continuity method, estimate replacement, or actual operational change. If multiple causes cannot be separated, leave the bridge unresolved. Never label a boundary expansion or contraction as environmental improvement or deterioration by itself.
